NOTICE
======

DS1Edit is a continuation of win_ds1edit, the Diablo II DS1 map editor written
by Paul Siramy. This file records where the code came from and the license
status of each part. It ships next to LICENSE in every release package.


1. win_ds1edit by Paul Siramy (2002-2011)
-----------------------------------------

Paul Siramy wrote ds1edit / win_ds1edit, the WYSIWYG DS1 editor the Diablo II
modding community has relied on since 2002: the DS1, DT1, DCC, DC6, COF and
AnimData.d2 format handling, the tile / object / path editing model, the
preview renderer, the undo system, and the on-line documentation and
tutorials. This project started from his last source release:

    win_ds1edit_20111030_src.zip  (5 November 2011, 25,326 lines)
    http://paul.siramy.free.fr/_divers/ds1/dl_ds1edit.html
    http://paul.siramy.free.fr/_divers/ds1/doc/index.html
    https://d2mods.info/forum/viewtopic.php?t=44  (ds1edit thread, 2002-)

License status. Neither that archive nor Paul's site carries a license text
or a copyright notice; the only document in the archive, "README FIRST.txt",
gives build instructions. Paul published the source next to every binary from
2002 onward, and in April 2003 noted on the Phrozen Keep that he had "released
the sources of my editor since 1 year now" and that no other editor had yet
been built from them. DS1Edit uses his code on that basis, with this
attribution. The MIT license in LICENSE is granted by Ben Ethington for the
modifications and additions made in this project; it is not a relicensing of
Paul's original work, which remains his. If you are Paul and would like the
attribution or terms stated differently, open an issue at
https://github.com/bethington/d2-ds1-edit and it will be changed.

