Every one of these has been modified, some heavily, for the Allegro 4 -> 5
port and the work since; each carries a short header pointing back here.
Files not listed (src/cli/, src/core/compose_*, src/core/mpq_index*,
src/core/palette.c, src/core/rgba_cache.c, most of src/ui/, the tests and the
CMake build) are new to this project.

The user guides under docs/01-Getting-Started, docs/02-Tutorials,
docs/03-Advanced-Guides and docs/04-Examples are Paul's original documentation
and tutorials (http://paul.siramy.free.fr/_divers/ds1/doc/index.html),
converted to Markdown. docs/README.txt is his original readme.


2. Stormless MPQ sample code by Tom Amigo (2000)
------------------------------------------------

src/mpq/ (Dcl_tbl.c, Dclib.h, Explode.c, MpqView.c, MpqView.h, Wav_unp.c,
Wav_unp.h, mpqtypes.h) is the "Sample Console App source code" that Tom Amigo
published with the Stormless MPQ Editor at http://www.angelfire.com/sc/mpq/
(August 2000), as adapted by Paul Siramy for win_ds1edit ("I needed very few
minor modifications to suit my needs" -- README FIRST.txt). Tom Amigo released
it so that others could learn the MPQ format and build on it; no license text
accompanies it.


